{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-02-Jul-2024-Shift4.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "In ∆ABC the straight line parallel to the side BC meets AB and AC at the points P and Q, respectively. If AP = QC, the length of AB is 12 cm and the length of AQ is 2 cm, then the length (in cm) of CQ is:", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Coordinate Geometry", "sub": "slope-and-line", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "At the beginning of day 1 of a month, Rajesh has 500 eggs. He sells 20% of the eggs by the end of the day and added b% of the eggs at the beginning of the next day and sold 20% of the eggs at the end of the next day. This pattern continued up to the end of the third day of the month when he is left with 1024 eggs. The value of b is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "500", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹4,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5,987", "added": false}, {"text": "4,520", "added": false}, {"text": "6,993", "added": false}, {"text": "7,052", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "L and M are the mid points of sides AB and AC of a triangle ABC, respectively, and BC = 18 cm. If LM || BC, then find the length of LM (in cm).", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "21% more", "added": false}, {"text": "21% less", "added": false}, {"text": "19% less", "added": false}, {"text": "19% more", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "In an election between two candidates, one got 65% of the total valid votes. 20% of the votes were invalid. If the total number of votes was 7,500, the number of valid votes that the other candidate got was:", "options": [{"text": "1,700", "added": false}, {"text": "2,100", "added": false}, {"text": "4,300", "added": false}, {"text": "1,900", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "In ∆PQR, PR = 10 cm. Find the length of PT, where ST∥ QR. Given that PS = 6 cm and QS = 14 cm.", "options": [{"text": "2 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "1.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The radius and height of a cylinder are in the ratio 6 : 7 and its volume is 792 cm3. Calculate its curved surface area in cm2.", "options": [{"text": "490", "added": false}, {"text": "226", "added": false}, {"text": "264", "added": false}, {"text": "262", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "A sum becomes ₹6,600 in 4 years at simple interest at a yearly interest rate of 5% per annum. What is the sum?", "options": [{"text": "₹4,400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,300", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Divide some money in the ratio Ravi, Reeta and Rahul that 5 (Part of Ravi) = 3 (Part of Reeta) =11 (Part of Rahul). The money ratio of Ravi : Reeta : Rahul is equal to:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "What is the number of digits required for numbering a book with 428 pages?", "options": [{"text": "1176", "added": false}, {"text": "1500", "added": false}, {"text": "2000", "added": false}, {"text": "988", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "factors-divisors", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "In June, Rohit’s bank account balance is ₹5,000 for 25 days, ₹20,000 for 2 days and ₹1,500 for 3 days. What is the average balance (in ₹) in Rohit's bank account in June?", "options": [{"text": "5575", "added": false}, {"text": "5650", "added": false}, {"text": "5200", "added": false}, {"text": "6000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "A man spends 35% of his monthly income on food and four-thirteenths of the remaining income on transport. He incurs some other expenses, but also saves Rs.6,300 per month, the latter being equal to 20% of the balance remaining just after spending on food and transport. What is his monthly income (in Rs.)?", "options": [{"text": "67500", "added": false}, {"text": "72,000", "added": false}, {"text": "70,000", "added": false}, {"text": "63000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "A, B and C can complete a work in 12, 15 and 20 days, respectively. How many days are required to finish the work if they work together?", "options": [{"text": "5 days", "added": false}, {"text": "3 days", "added": false}, {"text": "6 days", "added": false}, {"text": "4 days", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "In ∆EFG, XY ∥ FG, area of the quadrilateral XFGY = 44 m2. If EX : XF = 2 : 3, then find the area of ∆EXY (in m2).", "options": [{"text": "8.38", "added": false}, {"text": "9.46", "added": false}, {"text": "7.28", "added": false}, {"text": "8.10", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "paths-and-borders", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "-4", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "-3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "The triangle has sides 3 cm, 4 cm and 5 cm. What is the length of the perpendicular from the opposite vertex to the side whose length is 5 cm?", "options": [{"text": "2.4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "1.4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "2.2 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "The given line graph shows the number of scooters manufactured (in thousands) by companies X and Z, over the years. What is the average number of scooters manufactured by company X over the given period?", "options": [{"text": "126500", "added": false}, {"text": "213000", "added": false}, {"text": "256000", "added": false}, {"text": "116500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "line-graph", "key_answer": null}]}